  "review": {
    "verdict": "No actionable defect in the exact frozen eight-file patch. Original Windows failures are consistent with real SQLite observer or reopened store handles remaining open when the earlier registered fixture rm hook runs. Windows re-run is still required; local fixture evidence is not native Windows proof.",
    "lifetime": "One owner tracks every successfully opened DatabaseSync and SqliteStore; closes raw observers and all original/reopened stores before any rm. Failed store constructors continue to use unchanged production ownership rollback.",
    "closeFailure": "Cleanup attempts all owned closes, records original failure objects in AggregateError.errors, rejects before rm on any failure, and preserves the directory. It does not record a failed native close as physical release or overwrite the original failure.",
    "manualCloseAndIdempotence": "Raw manual close is recognized through isOpen; SqliteStore.closeAsync awaits unchanged closeCompletion after manual close. A previously failed store close remains rejected. removed is set only after successful rm; successful explicit cleanup then t.after is idempotent. A genuine raw close may checkpoint WAL, so preservation assertion uses logical schema rather than false byte-for-byte WAL immutability.",
    "existingIntegrityAssertions": "Original four files retain all 41 test identities, all 311 assertions and timeout/skip values. Only two future-schema assert.throws callbacks now call the tracked openStore wrapper around the same genuine SqliteStore constructor; DB_VERSION_UNSUPPORTED assertions and byte-equality assertions remain unchanged. All nine originally failing test bodies retain their integrity assertions.",
    "newRegressionCoverage": "Actual observer and reopened store lifetimes, manual close, repeated cleanup, open-after-removal rejection; actual DatabaseSync close method fault retains the exact original error and directory while closing other handles, then succeeds only after real close is restored.",
    "portableCISelection": "fixture-lifetime compiled test is explicitly in WINDOWS_STORAGE_TESTS; launcher test verifies inclusion and existing non-POSIX selection exclusions. Native Job Object test remains its existing skipped unsupported lane.",
    "production": "No production storage close or command backend source changes in this patch; no new Windows native Job Object capability claim, timeout relaxation, skip widening, or filesystem removal retry/error swallowing.",
    "concurrencyScope": "Helper is used as one fixture-owned teardown and awaited explicit cleanup; no new promise scheduling or inter-test global connection ownership."
  },
